                    \\{f, g\} = H_f g = \omega(H_f, H_g).
            %p
              See
              %a{:href => "PresymplecticManifolds"} below
              for more. However, such Poisson manifolds are very special. It is a basic theorem that Poisson structures on a manifold are equivalent to the smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
